## (3b) provenance: first Step 4 shot crashed on a tool bug, then fixed and re-fired

The first execution of this Step-4 command against pid 13076 raised:
  frida.RPCException: TypeError: cannot read property 'Symbol.iterator' of undefined at dis (/script1.js:76)
Root cause: scripts/dis.js:76 rendered the hex column with Array.from(insn.bytes), but Frida's
Instruction object exposes no .bytes property (this was dis.js's first-ever live run).
Fix applied to scripts/dis.js (read-only, no new capability — see section 2):
  const hex = Array.from(new Uint8Array(p.readByteArray(insn.size)))
      .map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join(' ');
Re-uploaded to C:\ns\, sha re-verified (section 3), then the same command re-fired. The output in
section 4 is from that second, successful shot. Deviation from the plan's "一行都不改" note on
dis.js is recorded here: dis.js WAS changed (one line) and the change was authorized out-of-band.

