## (5) Step 5 — cross-validation live <-> offline (the real acceptance)

offline same window (count read as hex on this side, so 0x28 = 40 insns):
$ python3 scripts/disrva.py 0x1D08520 0x28
; stellaris.exe  .text RVA 0x1d08520  (40 insns)
  ...
  01d08577  call    qword ptr [rax + 0x10]
  01d0857a  dec     dword ptr [rbx + 8]
  ...
  01d085aa  add     rsp, 0x20
  01d085ae  pop     rdi

grep counts (all four must be 1):
  live  call [rax+0x10] : 1
  off   call [rax+0x10] : 1
  live  dec  [rbx+8]    : 1
  off   dec  [rbx+8]    : 1

live and offline meet on the same two instructions §26 quotes. Renderers differ (live prints a
byte-offset column + single-space mnemonic; offline prints absolute RVA + mnemonic padded to 7),
and the count bases differ (fridadis.py reads decimal, disrva.py reads hex) — hence whitespace-
tolerant grep -E, not a verbatim diff. Offline 0 decode failures.

